 "findings": {
  "low_level": [
   "The network is opt-W1's template recursion with the min and max exchange (T42) on the fp32 key twiddled to u32: 290 VIMNMX, 142 SHFL, 2 CREDUX.MIN, 16 VOTE, 30 POPC, 8 predicated STS in the N 128 k 16 latency kernel (two network copies), no BSSY, no BRA beyond the harness's five, 0 stack, 0 STL, 0 LDL in every warp cell (T36 check). Registers 30 to 64 in the latency kernel (W1_eager_same 24 to 59), 23 to 32 in the throughput kernel (40 at N 256 k 64), occupancy 8 blocks per SM (6 at N 256 k 64, same as the control). One-ballot recovery: one VOTE.ANY per slot (8 back to back at IPT 8), the popc sum compared with k, then a BSSY, predicated BRA region with the fast path (one POPC, one LOP3, one IADD, one ISETP, one IMAD, one predicated STS per slot) and the two-class pass with IPT more VOTE on the other side, BSYNC. The region spans the whole call (BSSY at the kernel entry of the call), 2 BSSY and 2 BSYNC per latency kernel. Level tile order with the truncated final merge. Registers 32 to 72 in the latency kernel, throughput occupancy 8 blocks per SM up to N 128 and 6 at N 256."
  ],
  "algorithmic": [
   "Against the eager order with the same recovery (N10_ge1_trunc, same lock section), prefer_smaller_index latency: N 32 identical (569, 507), N 64 812, 764, 729 against 809, 747, 712 (plus 3 to 17, same dependency graph), N 128 k 4, 16, 32 992, 960, 925 against 1085, 1053, 1018 (0.91x), N 128 k 64 942 against 944, N 256 k 4, 16, 32 1304, 1273, 1240 against 1893, 1862, 1829 (0.68x, 31 percent), N 256 k 64 1341 against 1453 (0.92x). Throughput N 128 318 to 329 against 313 to 323 (plus 1.5 percent), N 256 k 4 to 32 339 to 344 against 272 to 276 (plus 24 percent), N 256 k 64 261 against 263.",
   "Against the u64 word (W1_eager_same, through the same-session control chain): N 128 k 16 960 against 1918 (0.50x), N 256 k 16 1273 against 3826 (0.33x), N 256 k 64 1341 against 4650 (0.29x). The fastest fp32 prefer_smaller_index form measured at N 128 and 256."
  ],
  "negative": [
   "Nothing gained at one or two tiles (N 32, N 64), the level loop is the eager loop there with a few cycles of schedule noise against it."
  ],
  "surprises": [
   "The level order's throughput at N 256 flips from minus 4 percent (two-class recovery, batch 1) to plus 24 percent (one-ballot recovery) against the eager order at equal occupancy (6 blocks per SM): the eager one-ballot kernel schedules badly in the throughput regime, not the level one well."
  ],
  "open_questions": [
   "Whether the N 256 eager throughput loss is a register or an issue-order effect (the two kernels have the same instruction histogram up to the tile order)."
  ]
 },
